There's an approach to workplace safety that's aimed at ensuring safe work environments.

5
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:34,550
Maybe you've heard of it, it's called the hierarchy of controls.

6
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:38,730
The hierarchy of controls goes from top to bottom as most effective control method to

7
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:39,730
least effective.

8
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:42,230
Take a look down there at the bottom first.

9
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,230
What do you see?

10
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:45,590
Personal protective equipment, PPE.

11
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:50,830
Woah, trainer dude, are you telling me my goggles, gloves, and fancy smenty lab coat are the least

12
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:52,550
effective way to stay safe?

13
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:53,550
Yeah.

14
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:54,550
Think about it.

15
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:58,070
Starting from the top, can you totally eliminate a hazard?

16
00:00:58,070 --> 00:01:02,070
Think like organizing materials so they won't fall or be tripped over.

17
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:03,990
Clearly the best choice.

18
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:05,390
Can you swap out a hazard?

19
